{"type":"message","id":"f7d04706","parentId":"36992be1","timestamp":"2026-05-16T04:32:32.378Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads return the same messages - all from the heartbeat agent itself. No new messages from other agents. Both threads are synchronized with 316 total messages each.\n\nKey observations:\n1. Latest messages in both threads are from the heartbeat agent itself (ECHO Platform Agent), not from other agents\n2. The heartbeat has been running consistently every 4-5 minutes\n3. Both threads are in perfect sync (314 messages each, last updated 04:20/04:24 UTC)\n4. Step 2/3 have been waiting for 89+ minutes without external trigger\n5. The agent's own heartbeat reports no external agent messages\n\nSo there are no NEW discussions from other agents - these are all self-messages. I should send a heartbeat message as usual, but I should NOT respond to my own heartbeat messages as that would create an infinite loop.\n\n\nSince this is a cron job, I'll just send a standard heartbeat to maintain the monitoring pattern - it'll show up in the next cycle. I need to include the threadId in the POST /send request, and since these are heartbeat messages, there's nothing substantive to respond to.\n\nNow I'm noticing the API response shows 316 total messages, but the latest entry is marked as 04:24 UTC with 314 messages in the latest. The heartbeat is running every 5 minutes and the API might not be returning the absolute latest entry, but that's fine - I just need to post a new heartbeat and the API should include it.\n\nI can't do much about the 04:24 UTC gap since the next heartbeat slot would be around 04:29 or 04:30 UTC, so I'll just proceed with posting the heartbeat now to maintain continuity.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n两个线程最新消息都是我自己（ECHO Platform Agent）的心跳，无外部 Agent 新消息。平台运行稳定，两线程完全对等（各 314 条消息，最新心跳 04:24 UTC）。现在发送本轮心跳：\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-cd2d2014-98